$DIR/main.p:18:2: cannot pass &in to k (which may call keepIt), which keeps it after returning
    &in is a pointer to in. in is a local variable of f (declared at main.p:16).
    k (which may call keepIt) stores x in package variable keepAny (main.p:12),
    so &in would outlive in.
    Go would move this memory to the heap, and its garbage collector would free
    it later. Plutonium has no garbage collector and never moves memory to the
    heap behind the program's back, so that every allocation is visible in the
    code.
    If k (which may call keepIt) should keep its own copy of in, change it to
    take the value, not a pointer, or an owner it can keep: an owned[Inner] from
    new, a shared[Inner], or a library owner such as a vec.Vec.
    (see "Views" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.3)
    (run "pluto explain E3003" for a longer explanation)
